= Research on Pressure Effects

== Abstract

This study examines the effect of pressure on reaction rates in aqueous solutions.
The experiment involved sixty participants across four experimental conditions.

== Introduction

Chemistry is the science of matter and its transformations at the molecular level.
Reaction kinetics describes how quickly chemical reactions proceed over time.
Pressure is known to influence reaction rates by changing activation volumes.

== Methods

Samples were prepared at three pressures: 1, 2, and 4 atmospheres.
Each trial lasted forty-five minutes with constant stirring.
Measurements were recorded every ten seconds throughout the trial.

== Results

The average reaction rate at 1 atm was 0.05 mol per litre per second.
At 2 atm the rate increased moderately to 0.11 mol per litre per second.
The highest pressure of 4 atm yielded a rate of 0.29 mol per litre per second.

== Conclusion

Pressure has a moderate positive effect on reaction rates in this system.
Future work should investigate the combined effect of pressure and temperature.
